# git worktrees checked out inside the repo (a live checkout, never content).
# Root-anchored: an unanchored `worktrees/` matches that directory name at ANY
# depth, and a gitignored path is invisible to `git ls-files`, which is how
# tests/repo_sources.py enumerates every guardrail's input. So the loose form
# would silently drop a real `server/worktrees/` out of the seam checks rather
# than merely hiding it from `git status`.
/worktrees/
